ai-sandbox/personal-website/

# academic_notes/ is now its own separate git repo (same pattern as
# personal-website/ above), so the tablet's Obsidian gitsync plugin can
# clone/sync just this lightweight subtree instead of the whole,
# increasingly large academic-hub vault. See the app.json
# userIgnoreFilters entry alongside this for the matching Obsidian-side
# exclusion (added 2026-09-08).
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/academic_notes/

# academic-hub/**/textbooks-and-papers/ (or its newer name, textbooks/ --
# see the 2026-08-31 note below) holds actual copyrighted published
# textbooks (PDFs) and their full-text Markdown conversions -- these
# specific patterns are ignored to avoid uploading large files and
# IP-protected text (deny-list, not a blanket directory ignore: negating
# individual files back out of a fully-excluded directory tree is a known
# git gitignore pitfall -- a parent directory match blocks descent into it
# regardless of later "!" rules on files inside).
#
# Fixed 2026-08-31 (first pass): this used to match academic-hub/**/*.md
# unscoped, which also silently excluded academic_notes/ -- the user's own
# TA notes, problem sets, exams, and handwritten-note transcriptions. Those
# aren't third-party copyrighted material and were never meant to be
# excluded; only the textbook-holding subtree needs protecting.
#
# Fixed again same day (second pass): the first-pass fix matched only the
# literal folder name "textbooks-and-papers", which broke the moment
# math-camp's copy of that folder got renamed to "textbooks" -- confirmed
# live, this silently would have let Book of Proof.pdf, Axler, and their
# full-text .md conversions become trackable again. Every course has since
# been renamed to "textbooks" (confirmed 2026-09-07), but both patterns stay
# matched explicitly rather than guessing at a single "current" name --
# confirmed, not assumed, per this repo's usual standard.
#
# academic_resources/'s lecture-slides/ and lecture-recordings/ are
# precautionary-protected too as of this same fix: real PDF files were
# found sitting in math-camp/lecture-slides/ during this investigation,
# and those are plausibly institution/professor-owned rather than the
# user's own authorship -- unconfirmed either way, so this defaults to
# protecting until the user explicitly says otherwise, not the reverse.
#
# Everything else under academic-hub -- scripts, the source-indexer's
# file-level .index/ cards, per-book _metadata.json, _image_descriptions.json,
# marker's run_config.json, and academic_notes/'s own .md output -- is
# either a derivative (titles/summaries/tags, not the original prose) or the
# user's own authored content, not a reproduction of copyrighted text, and
# stays tracked.
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/textbooks-and-papers/**/*.pdf
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/textbooks-and-papers/**/*.md
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/textbooks-and-papers/**/images/
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/textbooks/**/*.pdf
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/textbooks/**/*.md
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/textbooks/**/images/
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/lecture-slides/
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/lecture-recordings/
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/*_pages_cache.json
# Raw notebook source (OneNote), not a derivative index/metadata file --
# treated the same as the source PDFs, not tracked.
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/*.one
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/*.onetoc2
# Passage-level chunks (.index/chunks/) are NOT the same category as the
# file-level cards above -- each chunk stores verbatim excerpted text
# from the source (up to ~3000 chars) plus a dense per-passage embedding
# of that exact text, not an LLM-authored summary. That's a direct
# reproduction of copyrighted material, not a derivative description of
# it -- confirmed live this repo is public on GitHub, so this stays
# local-only and regenerable via `index_search.py chunk` rather than
# tracked (spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-29-passage-embeddings-design.md).
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/.index/chunks/

# research/journal-articles/ holds published journal articles (PDFs) and
# their full-text Markdown conversions -- same category of risk as
# academic-hub's textbooks-and-papers/ above (real, third-party copyrighted
# material), so the same deny-list treatment applies. research/'s other
# content -- independent-research/ (the user's own essays and research
# notes), and the source-indexer's own .index/ cards under research/ -- is
# the user's own authored content or a derivative summary of it, not a
# reproduction of someone else's copyrighted text, and stays trackable.
ai-sandbox/research/journal-articles/**/*.pdf
ai-sandbox/research/journal-articles/**/*.md
ai-sandbox/research/journal-articles/**/images/
ai-sandbox/research/**/*_pages_cache.json
ai-sandbox/research/.index/chunks/
# Visualization sub-agent output (.viz/) is derivative of corpus content the
# same way .index/chunks/ is -- gitignored by default rather than judging
# verbatim-reproduction risk per template/concept (academic-hub-status doc's
# IP posture).
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/.viz/
ai-sandbox/research/.viz/
# Broader, unanchored catch-all: generate_visualization()'s own default
# academic_hub_root=".." resolves to ai-sandbox/.viz/ when run from
# academic-rag-model/ (exactly what viz/README.md's own example one-liner
# does without an explicit --root) -- not covered by either named pattern
# above. This covers .viz/ under any current or future corpus root.
**/.viz/
# Combined-report output (.reports/) is the same kind of derivative,
# corpus-grounded generated content as .viz/ -- same IP posture, same
# any-root coverage rationale.
**/.reports/
# Extracted problem corpus (.problem_corpus/) contains problem text
# pulled directly from the corpus (textbooks, problem sets) -- closer to
# .index/chunks/'s "direct reproduction of copyrighted material" concern
# than .viz/'s generated charts, and gitignored for that same reason.
**/.problem_corpus/

#Prevent git workspace conflicts with obsidian
# Vault root is ai-sandbox/, one level below this .gitignore -- a pattern
# with a slash anywhere but the end (like ".obsidian/workspace*") is
# anchored to the .gitignore's own directory, not matched at any depth
# below it, so this needs the explicit prefix to actually reach the vault.
# Everything else under .obsidian/ (plugins, snippets, appearance.json,
# core/community-plugins.json) is tracked on purpose -- it's the vault's
# own config, not per-machine session state, so it travels with the repo
# when replicating this setup on another machine.
ai-sandbox/.obsidian/workspace*
ai-sandbox/.obsidian/cache
# Claude Code personal/local settings (not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local git worktrees (superpowers:using-git-worktrees)
.worktrees/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch workspace (ledgers, briefs, review
# packages) -- regenerable, not project output.
.superpowers/

# ==========================================================================
# LOCAL MACHINE / TOOL STATE -- secrets and per-machine config that must
# never leave this machine, as opposed to the copyright-driven exclusions
# above (found missing 2026-09-07: both READMEs already claimed ai-sandbox/.env
# was gitignored, but no pattern actually existed -- a plain `git add -A`
# would have staged a real GEMINI_API_KEY).
# ==========================================================================
ai-sandbox/.env
# Gemini CLI's own local settings -- same category as .env, not project content.
ai-sandbox/.gemini/
# JetBrains IDE project metadata -- machine-specific, not shared.
.idea/

# audio_generator writes each narration as a sibling <name>.mp3 next to its
# source .md, directly inside academic_notes/<course>/ and
# academic_resources/<course>/textbooks/ (see audio_generator/README.md's
# "Output" section) -- no dedicated output folder to scope a directory-level
# ignore to. A synthesized full-text reading of notes/textbook content is
# the same "derivative but verbatim-reproducing" category .index/chunks/,
# .viz/, .reports/, and .problem_corpus/ are already excluded for above
# (worse, in the textbooks case: audio of a copyrighted textbook's full
# text), and large besides -- excluded by extension since it can land
# anywhere under either tree.
ai-sandbox/academic-hub/**/*.mp3
ai-sandbox/research/**/*.mp3
